          "title": "Announcement: Green Future Youth Summit 2026",
          "content": "<p class=\"font-bold text-indigo-700 dark:text-indigo-300 mb-2\">GREEN FUTURE YOUTH SUMMIT 2026 — CALL FOR DELEGATES</p>\n            <p>Are you passionate (1) _____ building sustainable cities? Join over 500 high school students nationwide at the Green Future Youth Summit, taking place in Hanoi this July.</p>\n            <p class=\"mt-2\">Participants will attend hands-on workshops (2) _____ by leading environmental scientists and pitch real-world eco-innovations. Every delegate will receive a (3) _____ certificate and mentorship opportunities for community projects.</p>\n            <p class=\"mt-2\">To secure your spot, please submit your application form before May 30. Early applicants are strongly encouraged (4) _____ their project proposals in advance.</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "p_eng_2",
          "title": "Reading Passage: Artificial Intelligence in Modern Classrooms",
          "content": "<p>Over the past decade, artificial intelligence (AI) has shifted from a futuristic concept to an everyday educational partner. In many high schools, adaptive learning platforms now analyze how quickly a student solves a problem, identify subtle knowledge gaps, and generate customized practice exercises within seconds. Rather than replacing teachers, these tools free educators from repetitive grading so they can focus on mentorship, critical thinking, and emotional support.</p>\n            <p class=\"mt-2\">However, the rapid integration of AI also raises significant pedagogical concerns. Critics warn that over-reliance on automated writing assistants may weaken students' ability to construct original arguments independently. Moreover, unequal access to high-speed internet and modern devices threatens to widen the digital divide between urban and rural schools.</p>\n            <p class=\"mt-2\">To address these challenges, educational policymakers emphasize <strong>AI literacy</strong>—teaching students not merely how to prompt a machine, but how to verify facts, question algorithmic bias, and use technology ethically. When paired with thoughtful human guidance, AI can transform classrooms into more inclusive and engaging spaces for lifelong learning.</p>"
        }
